    <statement><p>Find the gradient of the function</p>
<p><m>f(p,q,r) = e^{\frac{r}{5}} + \ln\mathopen{}\left(q\right) + e^{p}</m>.</p>
<p><m>\mbox{grad} f =</m> <fillin characters="55" name="AnSwEr0001"/></p>
</statement>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>e^{p}\,\mathit{\vec i}+\frac{1}{q}\,\mathit{\vec j}+0.2e^{\frac{r}{5}}\,\mathit{\vec k}</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
    <solution><m>f_p = e^{p}</m>, <m>f_q = \frac{1}{q}</m>, <m>f_r = 0.2e^{\frac{r}{5}}</m>, we have
<me>\mbox{grad} f = e^{p}\,\vec i + \frac{1}{q}\,\vec j + 0.2e^{\frac{r}{5}}\,\vec k.</me>




</solution>
